title: 'Richer where filters: grouping, in, ranges, string operators'
status: complete
atomic: true
priority: medium
blocked_by: []
created_at: '2026-06-10T05:18:42'
updated_at: '2026-06-13T10:44:50'
result: 'Implemented richer where filters for stores. Statement-form `where` clauses
  now support: `field in [a, b, c]` (desugars to OR-chain of equalities), `field between
  LO and HI` (desugars to >= AND <=, consuming the ''and''), `field contains/starts_with/ends_with
  ''str''` text predicates on String fields, and parenthesized grouping `(a or b)`.
  Mixed and/or at the flat level is rejected with a clear "group with parentheses"
  error since the flat evaluator has no precedence.


  Threaded a new ast::FilterPred{Cmp,Contains,StartsWith,EndsWith} through AST ->
  HIR -> MIR name-mangling (store_filter_pred_str) -> codegen decode (parse_store_pred)
  -> eval_store_filter_pred/store_compare_field, adding store_text_predicate LLVM
  IR (memcmp prefix/suffix for starts/ends_with, scan loop for contains). Secondary-index
  fast path is disabled for non-Cmp primary predicates. Typer rejects text predicates
  on non-String fields.


  Added 7 conformance tests (store_filter_in_list/between/contains/starts_with/ends_with/grouping/in_query).
  Full test suite passes (1600+ tests, zero failures), zero build warnings.'
description: Item 9. Full boolean expression grammar in statement-form where filters
  (parenthesized grouping, and/or), plus in [..], between/ranges, contains, starts_with;
  lower to index/bloom probes when available via store_filter.rs.
